# Citation metadata for PyA3EDA (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as the repository's "Cite this repository" button, and
# Zenodo reads a subset of it when archiving a GitHub Release.  Keep it free of
# a `.zenodo.json` sibling: when both exist, Zenodo ignores this file entirely.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyA3EDA in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PyA3EDA: Python automation for Asymmetrically-constrained Adiabatic ALMO-EDA (A3EDA)"
abstract: >-
  PyA3EDA automates the full computational workflow for
  Asymmetrically-constrained Adiabatic ALMO-EDA (A3EDA) calculations in Q-Chem.
  A3EDA decomposes catalytic barriers into physically meaningful contributions —
  frozen-density (FRZ), polarisation (POL), and charge-transfer (CT) on the
  electronic-energy surface, plus an additional confinement (NI) term on the
  Gibbs-energy surface — revealing how a catalyst lowers or raises a reaction
  barrier.  A single YAML file drives input generation, local or SLURM
  execution, status tracking, extraction, and publication-ready plots.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Markus G. S."
    family-names: Weiss
    email: markus.guenter.weiss@rwth-aachen.de
    # CFF 1.2.0 allows one affiliation string per author; joint appointments
    # are conventionally written as a single semicolon-separated value.
    affiliation: "RWTH Aachen University; The University of Texas at Dallas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-2682-262X"
# Bump `version` and `date-released` in the same commit that bumps
# pyproject.toml, so the archived Zenodo record matches the released package.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/sterling-group/PyA3EDA"
url: "https://sterling-group.github.io/PyA3EDA/"
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - quantum chemistry
  - energy decomposition analysis
  - ALMO-EDA
  - Q-Chem
  - catalysis
  - automation
  - HPC
# The *concept* DOI: minted once, always resolves to the latest release, so it
# never needs touching again.  Version DOIs change every release and are listed
# under `identifiers` as they are archived.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22738497
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22738497
    description: "Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest PyA3EDA release."
